    static let text = "[Start here]\nWelcome to *[demo]. This song is a guide to everything in the app. Scroll through, and delete it from your songs whenever you like.\nEverything saves as you type, and syncs to every device you’re signed in on.\n\n[Writing]\nTap + to start a song. Give it a title, then write: every line is a lyric line.\nPut a section name on its own line in square brackets, like [Verse] or [Bridge]. Write your chorus once under [Chorus]. Next time, type [Chorus] and press Return, and it fills itself in.\n\n[Rhymes & words]\nThe rhyme bar above the keyboard rhymes with the word you just wrote. Tap one to put it in.\nRhyme map colours the words that rhyme with each other. Syllable counts shows how long each line runs, so your verses sit evenly. Both are at the top of the song.\n\n[When you’re stuck]\nMuse deals out quick prompts and exercises when the page is blank.\nLines writes rhyming next lines in your voice. Writing voice sets that voice: genre, mood and style. Listen to the whole song makes every suggestion fit what you’ve written so far.\nRate gives an honest co-writer’s read: a score, what’s working, and notes you can act on.\n\n[Ideas & voice memos]\nIdeas sits at the top of your songs. It’s a quick jot for stray lines, titles and concepts: tap + to jot one.\nRecord a voice memo the moment a melody turns up. When an idea grows, start a song from it.\n\n[Details & release]\nOpen ••• › Details for chords, key, tempo, capo, tuning and a status: Idea, Draft, Demo or Finished.\n••• › Credits keeps the writers and their splits, plus the release details: ISRC, UPC, release date and label. Once a song is out, Find Release looks it up on Apple Music and fills them in for you.\n\n[Audio & lyric sync]\nIn ••• › Audio, add each version of the song: voice memo, demo, mix, master. Tick the one that’s current. Stems, artwork and session files can live with the song too.\nSync Lyrics listens to the current version and times every line for you. Export .lrc saves the timed lyrics for streaming services and distributors.\n\n[Albums]\nGather songs into an album, EP or single with New Album, at the bottom of your songs. Its artwork goes on every song in it, and the album page shows how close each song is to finished.\n\n[Sharing & co-writing]\nShare sends a song as a link anyone can open, with its audio, or as an image of the lyrics. Share an album and it gets a page of its own, with every song on it.\nPick a username in Account so co-writers can find you, then invite them from ••• › Co-write. You can write in the same song at the same time, and see each other’s changes as they happen.\n\n[Perform]\n••• › Perform turns the song into a scrolling teleprompter for the stage or the studio. Set the speed and the text size, and it rolls on by itself.\n\n[Organising]\nMake folders, and drag songs between them. Swipe a song left to pin it to the top, or to delete it.\nOn iPhone, add the *[demo] widgets to your Home Screen: record a memo in one tap, or jump back into the song you were writing.\n\n[Keeping it safe]\nSave a Version in ••• › Details › Versions before big changes, and restore it any time. *[demo] also keeps one by itself when you come back to a song after a while.\nClean up tidies case, spacing and section tags, ready for streaming services. The original is saved in Versions first.\nCopy Lyrics from •••, or export every song from Account. On Mac, songs are also saved as files in Documents › [demo] Songs.\n\n[Common questions]\nWhere are my songs kept?\nIn your account, synced to iPhone, Mac and the web app at hellodemo.app/app. Each device keeps a copy too, so you can keep writing without a connection.\nWho can see my songs?\nOnly you, until you invite a co-writer or send a share link. You can stop a share link any time.\nHow do I get my songs out?\nCopy Lyrics from •••, export a song’s timed lyrics as .lrc, or export every song from Account.\nI changed something and want it back.\nOpen ••• › Details › Versions and restore an earlier version. Save one yourself before big changes.\nDo the AI features read my songs?\nOnly when you use them. Lines, Muse and Rate send what you’re working on to OpenAI. Turn AI Features off in Account and nothing is sent.\nWhat does Pro add?\nDemos, mixes and stems with 5 GB of space, voice memos synced everywhere, lyric sync, co-writing, share links, Lines and Rate in your voice, and Perform mode.\nWhere do I get help?\nAccount › Contact Support, or email help@hellodemo.app."
